		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Diabète sucré non insulino-dépendant</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">DID2</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">diabète sucré type II</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subclass of DIABETES MELLITUS that is not INSULIN-responsive or dependent (NIDDM). It is characterized initially by INSULIN RESISTANCE and HYPERINSULINEMIA; and eventually by GLUCOSE INTOLERANCE; HYPERGLYCEMIA; and overt diabetes. Type II diabetes mellitus is no longer considered a disease exclusively found in adults. Patients seldom develop KETOSIS but often exhibit OBESITY. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
