		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Endoglin (Osler-Rendu-Weber Syndrome 1) wt Allele</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Human ENG wild-type allele is located within 9q33-q34.1 and is approximately 40 kb in length. This allele, which encodes endoglin protein, is involved in endothelial cell growth regulation and may play a role in endothelial cells/integrin interactions. Mutations in the endoglin gene result in hereditary hemorrhagic telangiectasia. (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
