		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Immunoglobulin, hypervariable region</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Complimentarity Determining Region</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Hypervariable Loop</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Régions hypervariables</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">CDR (Complementarity Determining Region)</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Séquences CDR</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Régions CDR</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Régions déterminantes de la complémentarité</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">région hypervariable de l'anticorps</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">immunoglobuline, région hypervariable</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Three regions (CDR1; CDR2 and CDR3) of amino acid sequence in the IMMUNOGLOBULIN VARIABLE REGION that are highly divergent. Together the CDRs from the light and heavy immunoglobulin chains form a surface that is complementary to the antigen. These regions are also present in other members of the immunoglobulin superfamily, for example, T-cell receptors (RECEPTORS, ANTIGEN, T-CELL). (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0021054"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C1302678"/>
	</owl:Class>

