		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">DLT (Dépression à Long Terme)</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Dépression à long terme de l'excitabilité neuronale</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A persistent activity-dependent decrease in synaptic efficacy between NEURONS. It typically occurs following repeated low-frequency afferent stimulation, but it can be induced by other methods. Long-term depression appears to play a role in MEMORY. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;OrganOrTissueFunction"/>
	</owl:Class>

