		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">self help organization</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">mutual help and support group</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">mutual help association</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Support-group group each 60 minutes</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">suprt-grp grp ea.h</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">self-help group</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">groupes de soutien</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Groupes d'entre-aide</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Organizations which provide an environment encouraging social interactions through group activities or individual relationships especially for the purpose of rehabilitating or supporting patients, individuals with common health problems, or the elderly. They include therapeutic social clubs. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">organisme proposant un environnement favorisant les interactions sociales à travers des activités de groupe ou individuelles particulièrement pour rééduquer ou soutenir des patients, des individus ayant des problèmes généraux de santé, et des personnes âgées. Sont inclus les clubs sociaux thérapeutiques. (source : CISMeF)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0687744"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0030688"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C2148480"/>
	</owl:Class>

	<owl:Class rdf:about="&OntoAD;C0151744">
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Myocardial Ischemia</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">MyocardialIschemia</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Ischémie myocardique</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">IschémieMyocardique</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ischemic heart disease</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ischaemic heart disease</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">myocardial ischemia/hypoxia</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">IHD  Ischemic heart disease</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Ischemic heart disease or syndrome</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Ischemic Heart Diseases and Syndromes</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Cardiac ischemia</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">IHD</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ischemia; heart</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">myocardium; ischemic</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ISCHEMIC HEART DIS</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Ischemic heart diseases</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">ISCHEMIE DU MYOCARDE</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Ischémie cardiaque</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Cardiopathie ischémique</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Maladie cardiaque ischémique</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Cardiopathies ischémiques</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A disorder of cardiac function caused by insufficient blood flow to the muscle tissue of the heart. The decreased blood flow may be due to narrowing of the coronary arteries (CORONARY ARTERY DISEASE), to obstruction by a thrombus (CORONARY THROMBOSIS), or less commonly, to diffuse narrowing of arterioles and other small vessels within the heart. Severe interruption of the blood supply to the myocardial tissue may result in necrosis of cardiac muscle (MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION). (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Trouble de la fonction cardiaque provoquée par un flux sanguin insuffisant vers les tissus musculaires du coeur. L'écoulement diminué de sang peut être dû au rétrécissement des artères coronaires (Artériosclérose coronaire), à l'obstruction par un thrombus (Thrombose coronaire), ou moins communément, par un rétrécissement diffus des artérioles et autres petits vaisseaux dans le coeur. L'interruption grave de l'apport de sang du tissu myocardique peut avoir comme conséquence la nécrose du muscle  (source : CISMeF)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C1956346"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C1290384"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0878544"/>
		<OntoAD:has_severity rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0439793"/>
		<OntoAD:disease_has_associated_anatomic_site rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0007226"/>
		<OntoAD:has_finding_site rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0018787"/>
		<OntoAD:has_finding_site rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0027061"/>
		<OntoAD:disease_has_associated_anatomic_site rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0035237"/>
		<OntoAD:associated_finding_of rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C1313980"/>
		<OntoAD:has_associated_morphology rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C3266030"/>
	</owl:Class>

