		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Inhibiteurs des canaux du calcium</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Antagonistes calciques</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">inhibiteur calcique</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of drugs that act by selective inhibition of calcium influx through cell membranes or on the release and binding of calcium in intracellular pools. Since they are inducers of vascular and other smooth muscle relaxation, they are used in the drug therapy of hypertension and cerebrovascular spasms, as myocardial protective agents, and in the relaxation of uterine spasms. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
