	<owl:Class rdf:about="&OntoAD;C0023821">
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">High Density Lipoproteins</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">HighDensityLipoproteins</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Lipoprotéines HDL</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">LipoprotéinesHDL</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">high-density lipoprotein</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">alpha-Lipoproteins</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Heavy Lipoproteins</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">HDL  High density lipoprotein</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Lipoproteins, HDL</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">HDL</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">High densitiy lipoprotein</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">High density lipoprotein</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Lipoprotéine de haute densité</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">alpha-Lipoprotéines</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">alpha-Lipoprotéine</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">HDL (High-Density Lipoproteins)</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Lipoprotéines de haute densité</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of lipoproteins of small size (4-13 nm) and dense (greater than 1.063 g/ml) particles. HDL lipoproteins, synthesized in the liver without a lipid core, accumulate cholesterol esters from peripheral tissues and transport them to the liver for re-utilization or elimination from the body (the reverse cholesterol transport). Their major protein component is APOLIPOPROTEIN A-I. HDL also shuttle APOLIPOPROTEINS C and APOLIPOPROTEINS E to and from triglyceride-rich lipoproteins during their cat (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">classe de lipoprotéinesde petite grandeur (4-13 nm ) et dense (plus grand que 1.063 g/ml ) les particules. HDL lipoprotéines, synthétisé dans le foie sans un COEUR de lipide, accumulent du cholestérol esters des tissus périphériques et les transportent au foie pour la réutilisation ou l'élimination du corps (le transport de cholestérol contraire). Leur composante de protéine importante est APOLIPOprotéine A-I. HDL aussi la navette APOLIPOPROTEINES C et APOLIPOPROTEINES E à et de lipoprotéinestri (source : CISMeF)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0023820"/>
	</owl:Class>

