		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Neuro-psychologie</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A branch of psychology which investigates the correlation between experience or behavior and the basic neurophysiological processes. The term neuropsychology stresses the dominant role of the nervous system. It is a more narrowly defined field than physiological psychology or psychophysiology. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
