		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">M. de Gilles de la Tourette</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Trouble de Gilles de la Tourette</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Syndrome de Tourette-Guinon</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Gilles de la Tourette</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">association de tics vocaux et tics moteurs du syndrome de Gilles de la Tourette</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Forme associant tics vocaux et tics moteurs [syndrome de Gilles de la Tourette]</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neuropsychological disorder related to alterations in DOPAMINE metabolism and neurotransmission involving frontal-subcortical neuronal circuits. Both multiple motor and one or more vocal tics need to be present with TICS occurring many times a day, nearly daily, over a period of more than one year. The onset is before age 18 and the disturbance is not due to direct physiological effects of a substance or a general medical condition. The disturbance causes marked distress or significant impairm (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
