		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Protéasome 20S</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A large multisubunit complex that plays an important role in the degradation of most of the cytosolic and nuclear proteins in eukaryotic cells. It contains a 700-kDa catalytic sub-complex and two 700-kDa regulatory sub-complexes. The complex digests ubiquitinated proteins and protein activated via ornithine decarboxylase antizyme. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
