		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Insulins</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Insulin-class Agent</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Peptide hormones that cause an increase in the absorption of GLUCOSE by cells within organs such as LIVER, MUSCLE and ADIPOSE TISSUE. During normal metabolism insulins are produced by the PANCREATIC BETA CELLS in response to increased GLUCOSE. Natural and chemically-modified forms of insulin are also used in the treatment of GLUCOSE METABOLISM DISORDERS such as DIABETES MELLITUS. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0030292"/>
		<OntoAD:has_chemical_structure rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0021641"/>
	</owl:Class>

