		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">tomographe par émission de positrons</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A positron camera is a device intended to image the distribution of positron-emitting radionuclides in the body. This generic type of device may include signal analysis and display equipment, patient and equipment supports, radionuclide anatomical markers, component parts, and accessories. (source : SPN)</skos:definition>
