		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">os, SAI</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">hard form of connective tissue that constitutes the majority of the skeleton of most vertebrates; it consists of an organic component (the cells and matrix) and an inorganic, or mineral component; the matrix contains a framework of collagenous fibers and is impregnated with the mineral component, chiefly calcium phosphate and calcium carbonate, which imparts the quality of rigidity to bone. (source : CSP)</skos:definition>
