		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">agent de facilitation immunitaire</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">adjuvant</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Substances that augment, stimulate, activate, potentiate, or modulate the immune response at either the cellular or humoral level. The classical agents (Freund's adjuvant, BCG, Corynebacterium parvum, et al.) contain bacterial antigens. Some are endogenous (e.g., histamine, interferon, transfer factor, tuftsin, interleukin-1). Their mode of action is either non-specific, resulting in increased immune responsiveness to a wide variety of antigens, or antigen-specific, i.e., affecting a restricted  (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0876248"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0005525"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0301974"/>
	</owl:Class>

