		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Lymphoid Tumor</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neoplasm composed of a lymphocytic cell population which is usually malignant (clonal) by molecular genetic and/or immunophenotypic analysis. Lymphocytic neoplasms include Hodgkin's and Non-Hodgkin's lymphomas, acute and chronic lymphocytic leukemias, and plasma cell neoplasms. - 2003 (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
