	<owl:Class rdf:about="&OntoAD;C0025297">
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Viral meningitis</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">ViralMeningitis</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Méningite virale</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">MéningiteVirale</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Abacterial meningitis</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Viral meningitis,unspecifd</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Aseptic meningitis, viral</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">viral; infection, central nervous system, meningitis</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">virus; meningitis</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Meningitis, Viral</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">méningite aseptique virale</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">méningite non bactérienne</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Méningite virale, sans précision</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Viral infections of the leptomeninges and subarachnoid space. TOGAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; FLAVIVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; RUBELLA; BUNYAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ORBIVIRUS infections; PICORNAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ORTHOMYXOVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; RHABDOVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ARENAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; HERPESVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ADENOVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; JC VIRUS infections; and RETROVIRIDAE INFECTIONS may cause this form of meningitis. Clinical manifestations include fever, headache, neck pain, vomiting, PHOTOPHOBIA, and sign (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Infections virales des leptoméninges et de l'espace sous-arachnoïdien. Ce type d'infections peut être dû aux virus de la famille des Togaviridae (Rubéole), Flaviviridae, Bunyaviridae, Orbivirus, Picornaviridae, Orthomyxoviridae, Rhabdoviridae, Arenaviridae, Herpesviridae, Adenoviridae, JC virus et Retroviridae. Les manifestations cliniques sont : fièvre, céphalées, douleurs cervicales, vomissements, photophobie, et tout autre signe d'irritation méningée. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1996, Ch (source : MSHFRE)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0348165"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0729584"/>
		<OntoAD:has_severity rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0439793"/>
		<OntoAD:has_associated_morphology rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0021368"/>
		<OntoAD:has_causative_agent rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0042776"/>
		<OntoAD:clinically_associated_with rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0001175"/>
	</owl:Class>

