		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">ExtracellularMatrixProteinGene</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Extracellular Matrix Protein Genes encode mostly fibrous Extracellular Matrix Proteins (e.g., Collagen, Elastin, Fibronectins, and Laminin), typically located in the Extracellular Matrix and commonly involved in cell attachment, cell movement, cell growth, morphogenesis, organogenesis, and tissue repair, architecture, and organization. (NCI) (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
