		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Médicaments antidiabétiques</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Médicaments anti-diabétiques</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">préparation d'agent antidiabétique</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Any substance used to reduce hyperglycemia or treat disorders associated with diabetes. Based on their mechanism of action, this class of agents can be classified to the following groups: directly acting insulomimetics, which activates insulin receptors; indirectly acting insulinomimetics, which increase insulin release such as sulfonylureas or which potentiate the effect of insulin such as metformin; those act directly on the metabolism of glucose such as inhibitors of glucosidases and inhibito (source : )</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C2093625"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C2697970"/>
	</owl:Class>

