	<owl:Class rdf:about="&OntoAD;C2986691">
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Inherited bone marrow failure syndrome</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">InheritedBoneMarrowFailureSyndrome</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Syndrome héréditaire de défaillance de la moelle osseuse</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">SyndromeHéréditaireDeDéfaillanceDeLaMoelleOsseuse</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">IBMFS</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A rare disorder in which a person's bone marrow is unable to make enough blood cells and there is a family history of the same disorder. There are several different types of inherited bone marrow failure syndrome, and patients with one of them are at high risk of forming acute leukemia or certain solid tumors. (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
