		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">SerineHydrolaseGene</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The serine hydrolase genes encode a functional class of hydrolytic enzymes that contain a serine residue in their active site. The serine hydrolases can be grouped into subfamilies that contain closely related members in terms of substrate specificity or amino acid sequence similarity. (from OMIM 603156) (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C1334064"/>
	</owl:Class>

