		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A tripeptide that stimulates the release of THYROTROPIN and PROLACTIN. It is synthesized by the neurons in the PARAVENTRICULAR NUCLEUS of the HYPOTHALAMUS. After being released into the pituitary portal circulation, TRH (was called TRF) stimulates the release of TSH and PRL from the ANTERIOR PITUITARY GLAND. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C2699938"/>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C2015795"/>
		<OntoAD:gene_product_plays_role_in_biological_process rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0027793"/>
		<OntoAD:gene_product_expressed_in_tissue rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0020663"/>
		<OntoAD:may_diagnose rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0001621"/>
		<OntoAD:gene_product_encoded_by_gene rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C1335375"/>
		<OntoAD:contraindicated_drug rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0013182"/>
		<OntoAD:may_diagnose rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0032002"/>
		<OntoAD:gene_product_has_biochemical_function rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0020656"/>
	</owl:Class>

