		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Paralysie cérébrale spastique diplégique</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of cerebral palsy characterized by spasticity and hypertonia of the lower extremities bilaterally, particularly the legs, hips, and pelvis; this is the most common (70%) form of cerebral palsy. (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
