	<owl:Class rdf:about="&OntoAD;C0032273">
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Pneumoconiosis</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">Pneumoconiosis</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pneumoconiose</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">Pneumoconiose</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">PK  Pneumoconiosis</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">lung; fibrosis, with pneumoconiosis</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Pneumoconiose, sans précision</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A diffuse parenchymal lung disease caused by inhalation of dust and by tissue reaction to their presence. These inorganic, organic, particulate, or vaporized matters usually are inhaled by workers in their occupational environment, leading to the various forms (ASBESTOSIS; BYSSINOSIS; and others). Similar air pollution can also have deleterious effects on the general population. (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
