		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Déficit en thiamine</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">paralysie de Chastek</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Carence en thiamine, sans précision</skos:altLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A nutritional condition produced by a deficiency of THIAMINE in the diet, characterized by anorexia, irritability, and weight loss. Later, patients experience weakness, peripheral neuropathy, headache, and tachycardia. In addition to being caused by a poor diet, thiamine deficiency in the United States most commonly occurs as a result of alcoholism, since ethanol interferes with thiamine absorption. In countries relying on polished rice as a dietary staple, BERIBERI prevalence is very high. (Fro (source : MSH)</skos:definition>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0042850"/>
		<OntoAD:has_severity rdf:resource="&OntoAD;C0439793"/>
	</owl:Class>

