	<owl:Class rdf:about="&OntoAD;C1334706">
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Metalloproteinase Gene</skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">MetalloproteinaseGene</skos:hiddenLabel>
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en">Metalloproteinase Genes encode Metalloproteinases (endopeptidases) that use a metal ion, normally zinc, in the catalytic process and preferentially cleave the Gln-Gly peptide bond. Metalloproteinases are inactivated by metal chelators. (NCI) (source : NCI)</skos:definition>
